────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  SUMMARY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  This iteration measures the quality of BLIS's Pareto search algorithm against exhaustive ground truth (all 1,800 configurations), and tests whether expanding Phase 1 to include balanced block_size=32 coverage across all 15 GPU tiers improves Pareto recall. A random sampling baseline validates that the search's structure provides genuine advantage over naive exploration.

  * Three experiment arms: (1) exhaustive enumeration of all 1,800 configs to establish ground truth Pareto front, (2) comparison of search v1 (iter-1, 96% bs=16 bias) vs search v2 (balanced bs=16/bs=32 Phase 1) on Pareto recall, and (3) uniform random sampling of 200 configs as a negative control — all run across seeds {42, 123, 999}.
  * h-main predicts v2 achieves strictly higher Pareto recall than v1 because block_size=32 halves the KV preemption threshold (in blocks), and v1's Phase 1 only seeds 3 of 15 GPU tiers with bs=32 configs. The mechanism is well-specified: kv=3000,bs=32 yields 96K tokens (0 preemptions, rps=16.28) while kv=3000,bs=16 yields only 48K tokens (108 preemptions, rps=13.53).
  * h-control-negative predicts random sampling of 200 configs produces strictly lower recall than both v1 and v2, validating that tier-aware structured search adds value. If random sampling matches structured search, the Pareto front is trivially discoverable and the search algorithm's structure is unnecessary.
  * Confirmation criteria: v2 recall > v1 recall across all 3 seeds, with per-tier min-kv analysis as a more discriminating secondary metric. Refutation diagnostics are clearly specified: if v2 doesn't improve, Phase 2 neighbor expansion may already suffice or metric degeneracy may mask the difference.
  * Wall-time budget is reasonable: ~400s per seed for exhaustive (1,800 × 0.22s each), ~20s per seed for each search variant and random baseline. Total ~1,400s across all arms and seeds.
  * The only code change is to search.py Phase 1: adding 4 bs=32 resource profiles (kv=2000/3000/4000/7500) and expanding explicit bs=32 tier probes from 3 to all 15 GPU tiers, while keeping the 40% Phase 1 budget. This is a minimal, well-scoped change directly tied to the hypothesis.

